  "details": "Basically, locomotion doesn't turn itself back off after returning to full-body tracking from half-body (even though it says it's off in the menu).\n\nSteps to replicate:\n\n1. Use full-body trackers and have locomotion turned \"off\".\n\n2. Lose connection of trackers and go to half-body (locomotion is activated).\n\n3. Reconnect trackers (locomotion is not disactivated again, even though it is still shown as \"off\" in the tracking & IK menu).\n\nCan disable locomotion again by turning locomotion \"on\" and \"off\" again in settings but this a bit tedious.\n\nI am only able to confirm this issue exists on PC VR but, due to the nature of it, I assume it also exists in the other versions as well.\n\nI'm also not sure when I first noticed this problem but I'm sure it goes back much further than the current build number I used in this report.",
